<Doc title="Built on Postiz — PostDelegate" description="PostDelegate is built on the open-source Postiz publishing platform. Learn how the project and hosted services differ." h1="Built on Postiz. Operated as PostDelegate." eyebrow="Our foundation" lead="The open-source Postiz project provides the publishing foundation for our independently operated service.">
  <a slot="actions" href={SITE.signup} class="button">Create a workspace</a>
  <a slot="actions" href="https://github.com/gitroomhq/postiz-app" class="button button-outline" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Visit the upstream project</a>
  <h2>The shared foundation</h2>
  <p>PostDelegate uses a modified version of Postiz for its calendar, composer, media and publishing workflows. Its open-source architecture gives us a substantial foundation for the service we operate.</p>
  <h2>Two independently operated services</h2>
  <p><a href="https://postiz.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Postiz Cloud</a> is operated by the Postiz team. PostDelegate has its own operator, deployment, support, policies and channel rollout. A feature or integration offered on Postiz Cloud is not a promise of availability on PostDelegate.</p>
  <h2>Where to find the source</h2>
  <p>The <a href={SITE.source}>source for our modified application</a> is available under AGPL-3.0. See the <a href="https://github.com/gitroomhq/postiz-app" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">upstream repository</a> for the original project and its contributors.</p>
  <h2>What to check before choosing</h2>
  <ul><li>Whether your required channels can connect and publish.</li><li>The features enabled in the hosted service you are considering.</li><li>Its current support, subscription and data-handling terms.</li></ul>
  <p>PostDelegate is not affiliated with or endorsed by Postiz.</p>
</Doc>
